From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 11:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtl837x: serialize indirect register commands

Serialize complete PHY, OCP and SerDes commands and RMW operations.
Check write-data errors, keep bounded ITA access and handle zero masks.

Split from:
  package/kernel/rtl837x/patches/100-migrate-local-behavior-to-upstream-regmap.patch ([PATCH] rtl837x: migrate local board and forwarding policy to regmap)

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/rtl837x_common.c
+++ b/src/rtl837x_common.c
@@ -240,10 +240,12 @@
 
 int rtl837x_reg_bits_write(struct rtl837x_priv *priv, u32 reg, u32 mask, u32 val)
 {
+	if (!mask)
+		return 0;
 	return regmap_update_bits(priv->map, reg, mask, (val << __ffs(mask)) & mask);
 }
 
-int rtl837x_phy_read_c45(struct rtl837x_priv *priv, int phy, int devad, int regnum, u16 *pval)
+static int __rtl837x_phy_read_c45(struct rtl837x_priv *priv, int phy, int devad, int regnum, u16 *pval)
 {
